            "text": "The heating element sits under the cup and around its wall, so the tobacco warms from below and from the sides at once. The plate in the cap closes the chamber from above and keeps the heat on the load, the way a lid keeps it in a classic bowl.",
            "small": "Cross-section, not to scale",
            "more1_h": "Even from edge to center",
            "more1_p": "Heat reaches the whole load at once instead of burning the top layer, so the first draw and the last taste the same.",
